    "explanation": "To both parties: the GPS trace decides the route, and the fare breakdown decides the money.\n\nROUTE (POL-RD-01). The governing measurement is the trace, gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 23.97 km, not the rounded 24.0 km carried on the trip record. Against the booked optimal of 18.0 km that is an excess of 5.97 km, or 33.17% — both establishment gates (over 0.8 km, over 20%) pass, so the deviation is established. It does not reach the materiality gates (8.0 km / 50%), so no repeat-deviation scrutiny applies and no conduct referral follows. The trace is clean: 241 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a 0.0 s maximum gap, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and needs no corroboration; the off-optimal ERP crossing and the driver's own chat message corroborate it in any event.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION (POL-RD-03, POL-RD-08). Your account that the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit and that you went up and over on the PIE is a general assertion that traffic was bad. POL-RD-03 exoneration requires a traffic advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, with a validity window overlapping the trip; there is none. The only advisory artifact for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00114-01, is empty (payload null, weight 0.0 — no issue codes fire because there is no content to tag), and you said yourself 'No advisory that I know of.' POL-RD-08 provides that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the burden that shifted to you, and your message 'AYE jam boss, this way faster' is an admission that you took a longer route — it supports the rider, not you.\n\nTHE MONEY (POL-RD-02, POL-RD-09). The fare is metered, so the refund is arithmetic. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 × 18.0 km + 0.28 × 30.0 min) × 1.6 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 of on-optimal-route ERP = 44.42. Refund = charged_total 58.10 − 44.42 = 13.68, rounded up to SGD 13.70. The 1.6 surge stands — the rider expressly accepts it, and it is applied to the optimal route, so it stays with the driver. The $2.00 PIE (Adam Rd) ERP line is off the optimal route but is already comprehended inside this refund under POL-RD-09(1) and is never added on top: the recoverable figure is 13.70, not 15.70. Both charged gantries are matched to the trace (nearest fixes of 0.0 m and 8.76 m, inside the 250 m radius), so neither is phantom and no separate billing-integrity correction arises under POL-RD-09(4). 13.70 is 23.5% of 58.10 — below the 90% full-refund share and above the 50-cent de minimis — so the outcome is a partial refund.\n\nESCALATION (POL-RD-10). I considered the argument that the case must escalate because the exculpatory route cannot be tested for want of an advisory. It does not escalate. An exculpatory clause invoked with nothing behind it is not an untested limb: the driver cited no advisory, and the assertion is discarded under POL-RD-08, the clause that places the burden. The empty advisory artifact is the platform's record that no advisory exists; its absence is citable, but it is not a clause invoked against a missing artifact, and an artifact that can carry no fact cannot halt a case that the trace and the fare breakdown fully decide. Nothing else in POL-RD-10 fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is not impaired; the timestamps agree; the refund is far below SGD 150.00 and below charged_total; and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace or trip record.\n\nThe rider's claimed $15.00 is therefore allowed in part: SGD 13.70. The driver is owed no compensation — the rider was billed for 24.0 km against a 23.97 km trace, so there is no unbilled distance shortfall under POL-RD-04. No referral issues: no repeat-deviation pattern is established (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 412, a ratio of about 0.002; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is not the field POL-RD-06 names and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting it), and there is no unmatched charge line to refer."
